  "goodToKnow": "Die Nachkriegszeit is the post-war period, in Germany usually the years after 1945: rationing, the Trümmerfrauen clearing rubble, refugees from the east, the 1948 currency reform, and division into two states in 1949. The 1950s brought the West German Wirtschaftswunder (economic miracle). Nachkriegsarchitektur (post-war architecture) shapes many rebuilt city centres. It has no plural."
